{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430814-new-host-alert-cicadas-and-crabs","id":430814,"title":"New Host Alert! Cicadas and Crabs","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-06T16:55:54-08:00","id":430814,"title":"New Host Alert! Cicadas and Crabs","content":"Well, it seems Japan is host to two races of <i>shartha </i>we haven't seen before, taking advantage of the low Uratha population and the racism against them. Besides the Halaku, we now have the Alaghidim, the Crab Hosts, and the Sidalaaghu, the Cicada Host. The Crabs essentially run Odaiba and launch regular incursions into the bay, and the Cicadas show up around the end of their normal counterparts' waking cycle and turn the entire Shadow into a reenactment of <i>Starship Troopers</i> for a couple months (or given how this is Japan, maybe<i> Blue Gender</i>).<br /> <br /> So, I decided to create this thread to brainstorm what makes them unique, what their instinctual urge and Gauntlet Shenanigans are.<br /> <br /> Since I think Cicada Hosts are cooler, I'll submit the idea they have a larval form that sleeps in the Gauntlet until it's time to molt and breed. Their desire is to seek a way to extend their lifecycle, namely by creating manners in which humans may discover immortality. They don't care if the human has to hurt others to continue their life, the Host just want longer lifespans for their &quot;sponsors&quot;, so that they may study it in nymph form-and then take it in adult form. Naturally, they grow stronger the longer their adult form lives, but their lifespan is that of a normal cicada if unmodified. Ultimately, the way they seek to become their progenitor is to live long enough to grow to its vastness, and they are forever preparing for that day-one brood at a time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T17:23:17-08:00","id":430862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430814-new-host-alert-cicadas-and-crabs#post430814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Since I think Cicada Hosts are cooler, I'll submit the idea they have a larval form that sleeps in the Gauntlet until it's time to molt and breed. Their desire is to seek a way to extend their lifecycle, namely by creating manners in which humans may discover immortality. They don't care if the human has to hurt others to continue their life, the Host just want longer lifespans for their &quot;sponsors&quot;, so that they may study it in nymph form-and then take it in adult form. Naturally, they grow stronger the longer their adult form lives, but their lifespan is that of a normal cicada if unmodified. Ultimately, the way they seek to become their progenitor is to live long enough to grow to its vastness, and they are forever preparing for that day-one brood at a time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oooooo. I dig that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T09:43:01-08:00","id":431292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430814-new-host-alert-cicadas-and-crabs?p=430862#post430862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oooooo. I dig that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Holy crap, a developer praised me.<br /> <br /> Holy crap.<br /> <br /> I can start working on a writeup of the Cicada Hosts' biology and society...as compared to the crabs. What kind of thing would you associate with marauding crab demons...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T15:05:53-08:00","id":431812,"title":"","content":"I had a couple ideas. Mostly to do with their relationship with the gauntlet. Here are some spitballs.<br /> <br /> They bury into the guantlet for the winter months, and their moltings when they emerge poison the shadow.<br /> <br /> Their reaching through to the Flesh takes a long time (months).<br /> <br /> They can only come through it during the summer because they're offshoots of a Summer/Fire Spirit.<br /> <br /> They're the offshoots of one half of a twinned spirit, Winter and Summer, and they're looking for the other half so they can survive in the Flesh during the winter again.<br /> <br /> They reproduce by dropping hosts into the gauntlet for nymphs to feed on during the winter months, which fouls up the gauntlet with rotting carcasses and spirits.<br /> <br /> They want to change the resonance of their environs to something more palpable... hence all the noise. It's away to change the Resonance... maybe a Resonance of Silence. The loudest hosts being Hosts of Silence... heh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>All Things Strive.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4708-litheon","name":"Litheon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4708_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}